
Use webhooks as the primary trigger and periodic scans as reconciliation, with rate and capacity controls.

Create separate validation and release trust paths; unreviewed Jenkinsfile changes must not access
privileged agents or credentials.

Limit repository credentials to discovery and checkout; use target-specific workload identities for
deployment.

Apply branch and pull-request retention to jobs, build history, artifacts, and workspaces separately.

Require status checks for the exact merge candidate and monitor stale, duplicated, or missing events. Production Checklist

Webhook delivery, authentication, replay, and reconciliation behavior are tested.

Untrusted changes cannot alter privileged release logic or access protected resources.

Indexing duration, source API usage, event failures, and orphaned jobs are monitored.

Checks are tied to exact commit revisions and protected-branch rules.

Source credentials, webhook secrets, and repository permissions have owners and rotation procedures.

