stage('Deploy Staging') {
agent { label 'staging-deployer' }
steps {
withCredentials([string(credentialsId: 'staging-token', variable: 'TOKEN')]) {
sh 'set +x; ./ci/deploy-by-digest.sh "$TOKEN" "$ARTIFACT_DIGEST"'
}
}
}
}
}
Architecture and Operating Decisions

Pin build images and toolchains by digest or approved immutable version.

Use external registries for release artifacts and preserve source, Pipeline, test, SBOM, provenance, and
signature metadata.

Scope credentials by environment, job, agent, and duration; prefer federation over stored static secrets.

Promote one artifact digest through test, staging, and production without rebuilding.

Serialize environment deployments and require independent verification before promotion or completion. Production Checklist

Build environment identity and tool versions are recorded.

Container privileges, mounts, network, and registry trust are reviewed.

Credentials are short-lived or rotated, minimally scoped, and absent from logs and artifacts.

Artifact digest is identical across environments and visible in runtime metadata.

Deployment verification and recovery criteria include service and business signals.
